  "implementation_checklist": [
    "1. Copy warehouse_large_v1.xml to assets/scenes/warehouse/",
    "2. Update sceneXml path in warehouse-scenario.cc",
    "3. Set gnbTxPowerDbm = 30 (no change from current)",
    "4. Set gnbPos = Vector(-48, -33, 6), gnbLookAt = Vector(0, 0, 1.5)",
    "5. Replace rackSensorPositions with the 6 positions in rack_sensors[]",
    "6. Replace mobileRobotPositions and routes with the 5 robots above",
    "7. Update Bounds BoxValue to Box(-50, 50, -35, 35, 0, 2)",
    "8. Smoke-test: run isac-4x4, check mean_pathloss_db.",
    "   - If < 90 dB: Sionna finds too many strong reflections;      add 2 more rack rows (x=+44 and x=-40) or move sensors deeper into aisles.",
    "   - If > 115 dB: links too poor even for 8x8;      move sensors 8 m south (toward gNB) or remove 1\u20132 outer rack rows.",
    "   - Target: mean_pathloss_db in 95\u2013110 dB range across all challenge UEs."
  ],
  "isac_advantage_mechanism": "8x8 has a ~11\u00b0 beam. When a robot rounds a rack corner, the optimal path switches from direct to 1-bounce off a metal wall. Without ISAC, the beam scanner needs 1\u20132 s to re-discover the new best beam, causing a throughput dip. With ISAC, sensing detects the robot's new position and pre-steers to the reflected path BEFORE the dip happens. The narrower the beam the larger the miss penalty \u2014 so ISAC gain scales with array size, which IS the hypothesis."
}
